          "title": "You'll want to know: نشأ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نشأ — nashaʾa — \"to be reared, to grow up; to arise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نشأت أمي في قرية صغيرة. nashaʾat ummī fī qarya ṣaghīra. My mother grew up in a small village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: ينشأ, yanshaʾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of a problem or an idea: to arise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نشأ (nashaʾa) is built on the native Arabic root n-sh-ʾ (Lane), \"to come into being; to grow up\"; nashʾa is upbringing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
