          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسقط رأس — masqaṭ raʾs — \"a birthplace, a home town\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زرت مسقط رأس أبي في الصيف. zurtu masqaṭ raʾs abī fī aṣ-ṣayf. I visited my father’s home town in the summer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally the place where the head fell: where one was born."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسقط رأس (masqaṭ raʾs) is \"the place where the head fell\": masqaṭ is built on the native Arabic root s-q-ṭ, \"to fall\" (Lane), and raʾs, a head, is an inherited Semitic word, beside Hebrew rōsh and Aramaic rēshā (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
